@@ -1,5 +1,27 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.10.0
+
+### gdoc built in: work on a doc directly, not only sync it
+
+- **[gdoc](https://github.com/LucaDeLeo/gdoc) (MIT) is vendored** in
+  `src/gdoc_sync/_gdoc` at 0.23.0 and runs signed in with gdoc-sync's login.
+  Every gdoc command whose name gdoc-sync does not use works at the top level
+  (`cat`, `edit`, `suggest`, `comment --quote`, `revisions`, `cells`, `mcp`, ...);
+  all of them, including gdoc's `pull`/`push`/`diff`, are under `gdoc-sync doc`.
+  A shared name falls through to gdoc when only gdoc understands the options
+  (`diff --rev prev`, `auth --account work`).
+- **A linked Markdown file can stand in for its doc ID** in any gdoc command:
+  `gdoc-sync suggest notes.md "old" "new"`.
+- **`{>>comment:<<}` markers become anchored comments** through the Docs API
+  `insertComment` request when the OAuth project has it (Workspace Developer
+  Preview), falling back to the doc-level comment as before. New comments are
+  now posted after the push replaces the body, so the anchor survives it.
+- **`gdoc-sync hook`** for Claude Code: pull before an agent reads a linked
+  file, sync after it writes one, through the merge engine.
+- `scripts/vendor-gdoc.sh [REF]` re-vendors gdoc and re-applies
+  `scripts/vendor-gdoc-patches/`. New dependency: `requests`.
+
 ## Unreleased
 
 ### The same state file on Linux and macOS
