index af63c19..e5548a3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -119,9 +119,75 @@ gdoc-sync doctor           # confirms everything is wired up
 - **doctor** checks pandoc, config, the OAuth client, the token, and the API,
   and tells a new user exactly what's missing.
 - **link / unlink / open / auth / config** do what they say.
+- **hook** keeps linked files in sync around a Claude Code agent's edits — see
+  [Agents](#agents-claude-code-hook-and-mcp).
 - **rainbow** makes the first paragraph of any doc rainbow-colored. No further
   justification will be offered.
 
+## Working on a doc directly (gdoc, built in)
+
+`push` and `pull` move whole documents. For a targeted change — fix one
+sentence in a doc someone else owns, propose an edit, anchor a comment on a
+phrase, read last Tuesday's version — gdoc-sync ships
+[gdoc](https://github.com/LucaDeLeo/gdoc) (MIT, by [@LucaDeLeo](https://github.com/LucaDeLeo)),
+vendored in `src/gdoc_sync/_gdoc` and signed in with your gdoc-sync login, so
+there is nothing else to install or authorize.
+
+Every command takes a doc URL, a doc ID, **or a linked Markdown file**:
+
+```bash
+gdoc-sync cat notes.md --comments          # the doc as Markdown, comments inline, line-numbered
+gdoc-sync suggest notes.md "Q3" "Q4"       # a suggested edit the doc's owner accepts or rejects
+gdoc-sync edit notes.md "teh" "the"        # targeted find-and-replace (Markdown formatting allowed)
+gdoc-sync comment notes.md "source?" --quote "the Q3 numbers"   # anchored comment
+gdoc-sync revisions notes.md               # the doc's revision history
+gdoc-sync diff notes.md --rev prev         # what the last edit changed (word diff)
+gdoc-sync cat SHEET_URL --range A1:D20     # Google Sheets too; `cells` writes them
+```
+
+The rest: `info`, `tabs`, `toc`, `add-tab`, `insert`, `write`, `nest`/`unnest`,
+`comments`, `comment-info`, `reply`, `reopen`, `delete-comment`, `images`,
+`insert-image`, `replace-image`, `structure`, `ls`, `find`, `drives`, `new`,
+`cp`, `mkdir`, `mv`, `rename`, `cells`, `history`, and `mcp`. Each accepts
+`--json`, `--plain` or `--verbose`, and prints a short "since last time" banner
+on stderr (new comments, other editors) unless you pass `--quiet`. `gdoc-sync
+doc --help` lists them all with their options.
+
+gdoc's own `auth`, `config`, `diff`, `export`, `pull`, `push`, `resolve` and
+`share` share a name with a gdoc-sync command. The plain name runs gdoc-sync's;
+`gdoc-sync doc <command>` runs gdoc's, and so does the plain name when only
+gdoc understands the options (`diff --rev`, `auth --account work`). A second Google account: `gdoc-sync doc auth --account
+work`, then `--account work` on any command. gdoc's state lives in
+`~/.config/gdoc-sync/gdoc/`. It never updates itself; it is upgraded with
+gdoc-sync by `scripts/vendor-gdoc.sh`.
+
+## Agents: Claude Code hook and MCP
+
+**Hook.** `gdoc-sync hook` reads a Claude Code hook payload on stdin. Before a
+`Read` of a linked file it merges the doc's edits into the file (nothing is
+pushed), and after a `Write`/`Edit` it syncs the file both ways, through the
+same merge engine as `sync`, so a collaborator's concurrent edit is merged,
+not overwritten. Unlinked files are ignored; a conflict exits 2, which Claude
+Code shows to the agent. In `.claude/settings.json`:
+
+```json
+{"hooks": {
+  "PreToolUse":  [{"matcher": "Read",
+                   "hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "gdoc-sync hook"}]}],
+  "PostToolUse": [{"matcher": "Write|Edit|MultiEdit",
+                   "hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "gdoc-sync hook"}]}]
+}}
+```
+
+**MCP.** `gdoc-sync mcp` serves the gdoc commands as MCP tools over stdio
+(`gdoc_cat`, `gdoc_suggest`, `gdoc_comment`, ...) for Claude Desktop, Codex
+and other clients; `--read-only` exposes only the reading tools, `--allow
+cat,comments` a chosen few. Claude Desktop config:
+
+```json
+{"mcpServers": {"gdocs": {"command": "gdoc-sync", "args": ["mcp"]}}}
+```
+
 ## Tabs
 
 Google Docs can hold several tabs. gdoc-sync represents each one as a top-level
